How much of a tragedy it was for you, people of the Sharia and Persianate! Your lies! You wander everywhere to attract someone to your religion. Then you make him a father for a more intense sanctity than you are.
How much of a killing for you, oh continuers in the early morning! You say: 'If someone takes the promise with the direction of the mosque, then he means nothing, but if someone takes the promise with the direction of the silver in his mosque, then the promise is due.'" (Note: The original text contains untranslatable elements and references to specific cultural and religious contexts. The translation provided aims to convey the general meaning and tone of the original text, while acknowledging the inherent limitations in translating such culturally and contextually specific material.)
You are neglectful and despairing! What is more important? Is it gold? Or is it the mosque that makes gold forbidden?
You also say, "If one of them takes a vow in the name of the altar, it is nothing, but if one takes a vow in the name of the gift offered over him, the vow shall be binding."
O blind one! Which is more important? Is it the gift or the altar that sanctifies the gift?
So, whoever is promised in the name of the worshipper, is promised in their name and everything on that worshipper.
And whoever takes a covenant in the name of the mosque, takes a covenant in His name and in the name of what exists within it.
And everyone who takes the covenant in the name of the heavens has taken the covenant in the name of God's grace, which encompasses all.
How much it was an eye-opener for you, O teachers of the law and you, the prey! You are the ones who have been deceived! You give God ten percent of your harvest, of your mint, your cumin. But you have not followed the important commandments of God's law, such as justice, mercy, and truth. You should follow the last important commandments without assuming the first commandments."
You crippled guides! You remove the tiny insect from your food, but you eat a whole word!
How much of a tragedy it was for you, you people of the laws and the knightly code! Your lies! You clean the outside of the cup and the dish, but on the inside you are filled with jealousy. You desire only to satisfy your cravings.
My translation is a swallowed primary! Wash first the location of the ball and the belly, then the location will be washed flat.
How much of a tragedy it was for you, people of the Sharia and Persianate! Your lies! Like the towers called the White. They look beautiful from the outside, but inside they are full of the bones of the dead. They are also full of other unclean and filthy things.
This is how it is with you. From the outside, it looks like you are doing what is right, but on the inside, you are filled with things that are wrong. You show what you do not possess.
How bitter it is for you, you teachers of the law and you, yourselves victims! You are deceived! You conceal the secrets of the apostles. You conceal the secrets of believers.
And you say, "Indeed, we did not do what they did during the days of those who preceded us, those who killed the prophets. We did not seek assistance in killing the prophets."
